   <media:description>On March 6th, the Northwestern Center for Human Computer-Interaction + Design brought together researchers, designers, and artists to examine how generative AI is reshaping what it means to be creative. Symposium participants explored key interdisciplinary questions about human-AI collaboration, including how AI shifts roles within creative teams, how interface design can better support human intention, and what knowledge people need to stay in control of their creative process.</media:description>
